         globbing pattern _*_._s_h, and they are executable.  Any other files or
         directories present within the directory are silently ignored.

     ••   When a script is executed at boot time, it is passed the string
         “start” as its first and only argument.  At shutdown time, it is
         passed the string “stop” as its first and only argument.  All rrcc..dd//
         scripts are expected to handle these arguments appropriately.  If no
         action needs to be taken at a given time (either boot time or shut‐
         down time), the script should exit successfully and without producing
         an error message.

     ••   The scripts within each directory are executed in lexicographical or‐
         der.  If a specific order is required, numbers may be used as a pre‐
         fix to the existing filenames, so for example _1_0_0_._f_o_o would be exe‐
         cuted before _2_0_0_._b_a_r; without the numeric prefixes the opposite would
         be true.

     ••   The output from each script is traditionally a space character, fol‐
         lowed by the name of the software package being started or shut down,
         _w_i_t_h_o_u_t a trailing newline character.

